\b 5) Recommended Implementation Order\b0\par
\par
The platform is approximately 85% feature-complete with broad and advanced scope.\par
Top priority should be:\par
- Security and access control (auth, secrets)\par
- Production safety guards (LTP zero-block, exception middleware, panic close-all)\par
- Data correctness (real depth, real historical feeds)\par
\par
After that, move to UX velocity and trader productivity items (candles, charting, watchlists, toasts), then mobile parity, and finally infra scaling hardening.\par
\par
\b 6) Execution Plan (Recommended 4-Week Sprint)\b0\par
\par
\b Week 1 (Safety + Security)\b0\par
- Add global exception middleware and error envelope standard\par
- Implement LTP zero-guard in order pipeline\par
- Implement auth (JWT/session) for sensitive endpoints\par
- Add emergency close-all action with audit log\par
\par
\b Week 2 (Data Integrity + Trading Reliability)\b0\par
- Replace market depth random output with live depth source\par
- Harden historical/candle data sources to real broker path\par
- Track live execution costs and persist to execution records\par
\par
\b Week 3 (Frontend Productivity + Mobile Fixes)\b0\par
- Fix mobile missing API exports and env config\par
- Add toasts and loading skeletons\par
- Wire backtest comparison UI\par
\par
\b Week 4 (Scale + Foundations)\b0\par
- Start PostgreSQL migration path\par
- Add Redis cache for expensive market endpoints\par
- Establish pytest structure + smoke tests in CI\par
\par
\b 7) Risk Register (High Priority)\b0\par
1. Unauthorized trade execution risk (no auth)\par
2. Invalid-price execution risk (LTP fallback = 0.0)\par
3. Credential leakage risk (plain secret storage)\par
4. Data-quality risk (fake depth + mocked historical paths)\par
\par
\b 8) Definition of Production Ready\b0\par
Minimum acceptance checklist before real capital deployment:\par
- [ ] Auth required for all trade-affecting endpoints\par
- [ ] LTP and quote validity guardrails in execution pipeline\par
- [ ] Panic close-all tested in paper and live mode\par
- [ ] Exception middleware + structured logs + alerting\par
- [ ] Real market depth and historical data feeds only\par
- [ ] Smoke test suite in CI for critical flows\par
\par
\b 9) Quick Executive Summary\b0\par
FastTradeApp is already highly capable and unusually broad in scope (trading, analytics, Bloomberg-like terminal, finance suite, diagnostics, auto-trading).\par
Core engines are mature; the primary blockers are production safety and security controls, plus mobile parity and infra hardening.\par
\par
With the Tier-1 items completed, the platform can move from advanced prototype toward controlled production rollout.\par
